   "title": "GreatWhite brothers settle dispute as Mehul Shah’s family buys Hemang’s 50% stake",
   "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5"
  }
 ],
 "synopsis": "The ownership dispute at electrical goods maker GreatWhite Global Pvt. Ltd. has ended with Mehul Jadavji Shah’s family acquiring the 50% stake held by his younger brother Hemang Jadavji Shah’s family for about Rs 862 crore. The deal concludes Hemang Shah's 15-year entrepreneurial association with the business and resolves legal disputes brought before the National Company Law Tribunal in November 2024. Edelweiss Alternative Asset Advisors financed the transaction through a structured finance deal. The transaction places the company under a single ownership structure and follows an out-of-court settlement leading to the withdrawal of the company petition on October 9.",
